,"text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLInterchangeable":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLInterchangeable","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The interchangeable type is used to represent the second in a pair of interchangeable dual time signatures,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"such as the 6\/8 in 3\/4 (6\/8). A separate symbol attribute value is available compared to the time element’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"symbol attribute, which applies to the first of the dual time signatures.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLInterchangeable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLInterchangeable","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlinterchangeable","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLInterchangeable","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol"}}}